Fit it and check the diagnostics. How many parameters did you just estimate? Compare that with the number of data points.
Two things make this model identified: θ ~ Normal(0, 1) and a constrained to be positive. In your own words, what would go wrong without each one? (Hint: if you added 1 to every θ and every b, would the likelihood change? What if you flipped the sign of every θ and every a?)
